-- title:
--   Operation names for answer slots
-- statement:
--   The finite operation type for an answer slot is $$\mathrm{SlotOp}=\{\mathrm{test},\mathrm{fill}\},$$ where test names an emptiness check and fill names writing an answer. The bundle supplies decidable equality, a printable representation, a default element, and enumeration of this two-element type. For an arbitrary operation-label type $\kappa$, a slot-operation interface consists of an injective naming map $$\operatorname{charge}:\mathrm{SlotOp}\hookrightarrow\kappa.$$ The map identifies the operation's name in the surrounding cost vocabulary; it assigns no numerical price.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/meelgroup/arlib/blob/6262f60ad7556be62e94e87f6b5811cf299e7d94/Arlib/Computation/Slot.lean#L45-L64

